# This repo holds no scripts of its own, but it does hold workflow YAML that GitHub
# reads, and PNGs delivered by the Sync Assets pipeline in `brand`. Pinning endings
# keeps a clone with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) from rewriting
# them, which would show every synced file as modified on a clean checkout.
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.editorconfig  text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# templates/ holds files a new repo copies by hand. They carry a `.template` suffix so
# they do not apply to this directory, which also means none of the pins above match
# them. Without this line a Windows clone checks them out as CRLF, and copying one
# carries CRLF into the repo that copied it - defeating the very rule the template
# exists to spread (N6-CI-04, N6-REPO-04).
*.template      text eol=lf

# Two files that no extension-based pattern reaches. `LICENSE` is extensionless by
# convention, and a pattern for `.gitattributes` has to name it literally. Both still
# checked out CRLF with every pin above in place - verified by cloning with
# core.autocrlf=true and reading the bytes, not by grepping for CR.
LICENSE         text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Never apply end-of-line conversion to binaries. Without this, git would try to
# "fix" the endings inside a PNG and corrupt it.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.ico           binary
